{"source_object_ids":[1229182],"source_guids":["f81e293f-c597-416b-82ba-5c67e583cf96"],"matched_fields":{"DESCRIPTION":["data_center"]},"classification":"Dated permit from issued-permits register","description":"Low voltage control wiring for building automation systems (BAS).  This consists of wiring connections between the control panels and the devices and equipment that monitor the temperature, pressure and humidity of the building and rooms.

Work involves connecting plenum rated RS-485 communication wire, 18 to 22 gauge control wires and ¼” polytube from control panels to multiple temperature and humidity sensors throughout the data center.

These control wires will be installed in 3/4"-1" conduit and/or free hanging in ceiling plenum areas.  The low voltage panels and devices will be supplied by the owner.","work_classes":["Low Voltage - Other"],"parcel_pins":["045279612000"],"application_dates":["2026-09-04"],"final_dates":[],"snapshot_dates":["2026-11-15"]}

